US2010179835A1,Relating multiple electronic health records,"A computer-implemented method for alerting one or more members of a connected health network is provided, wherein the connected health network includes two or more members having linked medical records. The method includes receiving a change in a first health record of a first member, the first health record being linked to a second health record of a second member based on a specified relationship. The method also includes using the change in the first health record to determine whether a condition exists that could affect the second member, and, if so, alerting the second member of the affect of the change in the first health record on the second member.","['G06Q50/00', 'G16H10/60']","['G06Q', 'G16H']",29,1.0,US20230075466A1,"G06F40/205,A61B2034/2048,G02B27/01,A61B2090/365,G16H40/00,G16H40/67,A61B5/316,A61B3/00,A61B5/117,G06F3/00,G06F16/23,G16,G06F21/00,G06F3/011,G06F21/60,G10,G16H20/40,G06F21/6218,G06F40/20,G06F40/00,G06F3/013,A61B2034/2046,G02B27/00,A61B5/0059,G02B27/0093,A61B5/1176,G06F3/012,A61B2017/00017,G16H30/40,A61B5/339,A61B5/06,G06F16/2379,G06F40/279,G10L,A61B5/318,A61B2017/00216,G06F16/22,G06F21/6245,G06V20/20,A61B5/0077,G16H30/00,G02B2027/0138,G06F21/32,G06F21/30,G02B27/0101,G02,G,G02B27/0172,G16H40/60,A61B3/10,A61B90/37,A61B5/48,A,G16H,A61B2090/502,G02B2027/0127,A61B5/1171,G02B2027/0141,G16H10/00,G06F16/00,G06F21/31,A61,G10L15/26,G10L15/00,G02B,G06F,A61B2017/00207,G06F3/017,A61B17/00,A61B5/24,G02B27/017,A61B5/4803,A61B,A61B34/00,A61B3/0041,A61B3/0016,G16H10/60,G06F16/20,G16H20/00,G16H40/63,A61B3/113,G06V,A61B34/20,A61B2090/364,G06F40/289,A61B90/36,G16H80/00,A61B5/00,A61B2090/372,G02B2027/014,G06F21/62,A61B90/00,G06V20/00,A61B90/50,G06F3/01,G06","A wearable device can present virtual content to the wearer for many applications in a healthcare setting. The wearer may be a patient or a healthcare provider (HCP). Such applications can include, but are not limited to, access, display, and modifica