US2019159700A1,"Systems, apparatus, and methods for using a wearable device to confirm the identity of an individual","A wearable device includes at least one sensor for obtaining a unique identifier from the wearer when the wearer and for transmitting the unique identifier to one or more computer processors for use in determining whether the wearer is a particular individual. The wearable device may also include a wireless communications device for transmitting a signal (e.g., to a remote computing device) that confirms the identity of the wearer as the particular individual. A remote computing device, or other device, or individual, may then, based at least in part on receiving the signal, grant wearer access to a computer program, computing system, and/or a particular physical space.","['G16H40/67', 'G06F2218/00']","['G16H', 'G06F']",44,1.0,US20230153890A1,"A61,G,G06Q30/0255,G06Q30/02,G06Q30/0251,G16H20/30,A61B,G06Q30/0601,G06Q,G16H20/00,G06Q30/06,A,A61B5/103,G06Q30/0241,G16H,G16,A61B5/112,A61B5/00,G06Q30/00,G06Q30/0631,G06,A61B5/11","A retail enhancement system is disclosed. The retail enhancement system may include a sensor module configured to obtain a data about an individual during an athletic activity. The sensor module may be configured to be removably attached to a first article of footwear to be worn by the individual during the athletic activity. The retail enhancement system may also include an electronic device that is separate from the sensor module. The electronic device may be a dedicated device in a retail environment and may be configured to collect personal information about the individual, associate the sensor module with the individual, receive the data about the individual from the sensor module, determine a characteristic about a gait of the individual based on the data about the individual, and provide a recommendation about a second article of footwear to be worn by the individual to the individual.",[44],"G16H20/30,G16H20/00,G16H",,10,1.0
