US2014085077A1,Sedentary activity management method and apparatus using data from a data-capable band for managing health and wellness,"Data-capable personal worn or carried device can be used to detect sedentary activity for facilitating achievement of health and wellness goals. In one embodiment, a method includes receiving data representing an activity originating from a wearable device, determining the data representing the activity is a sedentary activity, and characterizing the sedentary activity based on a sedentary characteristic of the sedentary activity. Also, the method can initiate generation of notification alert information indicative of the presence of a value associated with the sedentary characteristic. In some embodiment, the method can cause a vibratory energy source in the wearable device to impart the notification alert information (e.g., haptically).","['G16H40/67', 'A61B5/681']","['G16H', 'A61B']",29,1.0,US20230153890A1,"A61,G,G06Q30/0255,G06Q30/02,G06Q30/0251,G16H20/30,A61B,G06Q30/0601,G06Q,G16H20/00,G06Q30/06,A,A61B5/103,G06Q30/0241,G16H,G16,A61B5/112,A61B5/00,G06Q30/00,G06Q30/0631,G06,A61B5/11","A retail enhancement system is disclosed. The retail enhancement system may include a sensor module configured to obtain a data about an individual during an athletic activity. The sensor module may be configured to be removably attached to a first article of footwear to be worn by the individual during the athletic activity. The retail enhancement system may also include an electronic device that is separate from the sensor module. The electronic device may be a dedicated device in a retail environment and may be configured to collect personal information about the individual, associate the sensor module with the individual, receive the data about the individual from the sensor module, determine a characteristic about a gait of the individual based on the data about the individual, and provide a recommendation about a second article of footwear to 