US2004010420A1,System for developing implementing and monitoring a health management program,"The method and system includes an integrated set of technology, scientifically-based algorithms and fitness equipment that: assesses a person&#39;s health, fitness and functional status; develops an individualized exercice program to address specific needs and improves limitations in health, fitness and function; monitors exercise program progress and adverse events; continuously adjusts exercise program progression in real time; measures changes in health, fitness and functional status; and reports exercise participation and changes in health, fitness and functional status to the participant, his/her health care provider (e.g., physician, physical therapist, psychologist) and health insurance provider. The method is also a vehicle for knowledge delivery of health education (e.g., nutrition, disease self-management, stress and time management), psychological coping strategies, and social support through integrated audio, video and web-based channels.","['G16H50/20', 'G16H40/67']","['G16H', 'G16H']",5,1.0,US20230153890A1,"A61,G,G06Q30/0255,G06Q30/02,G06Q30/0251,G16H20/30,A61B,G06Q30/0601,G06Q,G16H20/00,G06Q30/06,A,A61B5/103,G06Q30/0241,G16H,G16,A61B5/112,A61B5/00,G06Q30/00,G06Q30/0631,G06,A61B5/11","A retail enhancement system is disclosed. The retail enhancement system may include a sensor module configured to obtain a data about an individual during an athletic activity. The sensor module may be configured to be removably attached to a first article of footwear to be worn by the individual during the athletic activity. The retail enhancement system may also include an electronic device that is separate from the sensor module. The electronic device may be a dedicated device in a retail environment and may be configured to collect personal information about the individual, associate the sensor module with the individual, receive the data about the individual from the sensor 