US2010198605A1,Method for Structuring Balanced and Varied Meals,"The present invention relates to a method for structuring balanced and varied meals, and this method is characterized in that a database is constructed comprising all the varieties of dishes available during a given period, as well as the characteristics of their constituents, in that those dishes complying with the food restrictions relating to this user and constituting a balanced meal are selected from this database, for each meal, from among the available dishes, and in that the user chooses from among these dishes those that he or she prefers. The database consists of references of ingredients, of recipes, of dishes and of meals that are pre-established. These references are characterized in that each of the constituents of this database is coded as a function of its nutritional, therapeutic, budgetary properties, target consumers, etc. The filter of the database is formulated dynamically on the basis of the prior information and with the aid of the codes of the dishes (or meals). Stated otherwise, the inputting of the prior information serves to define requests.","['G16H20/60', 'G09B19/0092']","['G16H', 'G09B']",9,1.0,US20230153890A1,"A61,G,G06Q30/0255,G06Q30/02,G06Q30/0251,G16H20/30,A61B,G06Q30/0601,G06Q,G16H20/00,G06Q30/06,A,A61B5/103,G06Q30/0241,G16H,G16,A61B5/112,A61B5/00,G06Q30/00,G06Q30/0631,G06,A61B5/11","A retail enhancement system is disclosed. The retail enhancement system may include a sensor module configured to obtain a data about an individual during an athletic activity. The sensor module may be configured to be removably attached to a first article of footwear to be worn by the individual during the athletic activity. The retail enhancement system may also include an electronic device that is separate from the sensor module. The electronic device may be a dedicated device in a retail environment and may be configured to collect personal information about the individual, associate 