US2013303863A1,Patient Monitoring Apparatus,"A patient monitoring system including a sensing-recording device that attaches to a patient and a probe utilized by attending personnel at a trauma site. After an initial interaction between the probe and the sensing-recording device, the sensing-recording device samples one or more physiological parameters and stores time stamped readings in a first memory. The probe is adapted to take other measurements, download the data from the first memory of the sensing-recording device, manipulate the collective data and return data to a second memory in the sensing-recording device. The sensing-recording device continues to accumulate data in the first memory during transport of the patient from a trauma site to a medical facility.","['A61B5/00', 'G16H40/67']","['A61B', 'G16H']",34,1.0,US20230066299A1,"G08B5/00,A61,G08B,G08,A61B5/0022,A61B2562/00,G,G08B5/22,A61B5/01,A61B5/02055,A61B5/681,G06F,A61B5/68,G08B25/00,G08B25/10,G16H40/00,A61B5/021,G16H40/60,A61B2562/0219,G08C,G08C17/02,A61B5/7475,G08B21/0438,A61B5/002,A61B,G16H40/67,G08B21/00,A61B5/0082,A61B5/48,A61B5/1123,A61B5/6802,G16Z,A61B5/0002,A61B5/02,A61B5/1455,A63B71/00,A,A61B5/103,A61B5/6801,G06F16/20,G08B21/18,G16H,G08B21/04,G16Z99/00,A61B5/1121,A61B5/024,A61B5/1122,G16,A61B5/112,A61B5/0015,A61B5/1118,G08B21/06,G06F16/22,A63B,A61B5/1116,A61B5/4806,A61B5/74,A61B5/00,A61B5/145,A63,G06F16/00,G08C17/00,G08B21/02,G08B6/00,A61B2562/02,A61B5/0205,G08B25/01,A61B5/0059,G08B21/0446,G06,A61B5/11","In one aspect of the disclosed implementations, a device includes one or more motion sensors for sensing motion of the device and providing activity data indicative of the sensed motion. The device also includes one or more processors for monitoring the activity data, and receiving or generating annotation data for annotating the activity data with one or more markers or indicators to define one or more characteristics of an activity session. The device also includes one or more feedback devic